      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by using a **local secrets loader** that:\n\n1. **Reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file** at startup\n2. **Injects it only into the child process\u0027s environment** \u2014 specifically, the spawned Ingest agent process \u2014 immediately before that process starts\n3. **Never mutates the Hub\u0027s own process environment** \u2014 the Hub itself never holds the credential\n\nThis architecture means that even if the Hub process is compromised or behaves unexpectedly, it cannot leak the credential just by exposing its environment variables. The API key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs it (the Ingest or Query agent), not in the Hub\u0027s memory space.\n\nThe same scoping model is applied to the Query agent process as well.",
      "input_tokens": 5378,
